Step 2: Add the copy constructor: Point(const Point& p) : x(p.x), y(p.y) { cout << "copy "; }
Step 3: Add void show() const { cout << x << "," << y << " "; }
Step 4: In main: Point p1(3, 4); Point p2 = p1; p1.show(); p2.show();
Step 5: Point p2 = p1; is initialisation, so the copy constructor runs once before the two show() calls.

